{"id":1795697,"retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T18:19:27.884Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":18,"name":"Drama"},{"id":10751,"name":"Family"}],"homepage":"","id":1795697,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US","HK"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Graduation","overview":"\"Graduation\" is a poignant drama about 12-year-old Kai, who discovers his caretaker, Marie, unconscious in bed one morning, leading to her sudden death. As his family struggles with the aftermath, Kai uncovers the hidden truths about Marie’s life and death —truths that were invisible to the family until it was too late. Through its lens, Graduation calls attention to the often-overlooked role of domestic helpers in Hong Kong households, illustrating how these essential figures are rendered invisible despite their integral presence.  Kai, who sees Marie as a second mother, must navigate the complexities of grief, loss, and family dynamics, all while confronting the social structures that allowed Marie’s contributions to go unnoticed. In a film that explores childhood, family bonds, and the systemic erasure of domestic workers. Forced to face uncomfortable truths, Kai seeks solace in memory and ritual, finding that some truths, though invisible, can no longer be ignored.","popularity":0.0071,"poster_path":"/sf5tQpPIqx14Hpkeve0qp2y5bUz.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"HK","name":"Hong Kong"}],"release_date":"","revenue":0,"runtime":12,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Cantonese","iso_639_1":"cn","name":"广州话 / 廣州話"},{"english_name":"English","iso_639_1":"en","name":"English"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"Amidst his primary school graduation, a young boy, Kai, grapples with the sudden death of his caretaker, Marie, navigating the heavy emotional costs of growing up.","title":"Graduation","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[{"iso_3